      "title": "Australia news live: Wong speaks to Palestinian foreign minister about Gaza; Coalition defends plan to reduce First Nations content in schools",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/21/anthony-albanese-new-york-jim-chalmers-intergenerational-report-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow the day’s news live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Dan Tehan says fuel excise cut when oil price high a ‘sensible’ plan</strong></p><p><strong>Dan Tehan</strong>, the shadow minister for energy, said Gallagher’s criticism of the Coalition’s fuel plan wasn’t fair.</p><p>[What] I would say to Anthony Albanese and the Labor party is get out amongst the people and see what’s happening in your electorates because people are hurting because of cost of living …</p><p>We have the discipline to be able to do the policy work to make sure we can offset policies like this so it won’t be inflationary and it will provide much needed relief to people, and they need it now.</p><p>Obviously we’ve helped when the war started with some changes to the fuel excise but we’ve shifted, and [are] including in the budget, to providing more permanent cost of living arrangements, including through the tax system, to make sure that that ongoing cost-of-living help is there permanently, not just in these one-off arrangements, which, when we’ve got higher inflation, could be difficult in the economy.</p><p>Our decisions have been built and baked into the budget to make sure that that cost-of-living help is permanent. You know, the sooner this war in the Middle East stops, the better.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/21/anthony-albanese-new-york-jim-chalmers-intergenerational-report-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T02:02:09"
    },
    {
      "title": "More than 800,000 bees stolen across far north Queensland in ‘sophisticated’ operation",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/more-than-800000-bees-stolen-across-far-north-queensland-in-sophisticated-operation",
      "description": "<p>Apiarists will lose not just the insects but the value of pollination contracts, which can be worth thousands of dollars</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/21/anthony-albanese-new-york-jim-chalmers-intergenerational-report-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>An estimated 800,000 bees, worth tens of thousands of dollars, have been stolen from properties in far north Queensland.</p><p>The industry is already reeling from the <a href=\"https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-11/northernmost-incursion-of-varroa-destructor-mite-detected/107142280\">this month’s arrival</a> of the varroa mite parasite.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/more-than-800000-bees-stolen-across-far-north-queensland-in-sophisticated-operation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-21T00:00:29"
    },
    {
      "title": "Police allege mother behind Blue Mountains stabbing attack on three children that left one dead",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/police-mother-children-stabbing-attack-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Bystanders found all four on the side of the road at Valley Heights on Sunday with stabbing injuries</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/21/anthony-albanese-new-york-jim-chalmers-intergenerational-report-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Police have alleged that a mother was behind a stabbing attack on three young children that left one dead and two others fighting for their lives in hospital.</p><p>The woman, aged in her 40s, is also in a critical condition.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/police-mother-children-stabbing-attack-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-20T23:43:41"
    },
    {
      "title": "Albanese launches bid for UN security council seat and names former Murdoch aide to top diplomatic post",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/anthony-albanese-un-security-council-bid-siobhan-mckenna-news-corp-consul-general-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Australia and Finland are vying for a spot on the council, and the PM needs two thirds of member states to back him</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/21/anthony-albanese-new-york-jim-chalmers-intergenerational-report-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia having a seat at the United Nations Security Council will be able to help with the cost of living back home, the prime minister insists.</p><p>Anthony Albanese has launched a formal bid for Australia to serve a two-year term on the UN security council in 2029 and 2030.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/21/anthony-albanese-un-security-council-bid-siobhan-mckenna-news-corp-consul-general-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-20T21:45:37"
    },
