      "title": "ICE agent shoots and wounds man at traffic stop in Austin, Texas, officials say",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/20/man-shot-ice-agent-austin-texas",
      "description": "<p>Anti-ICE protests break out in push for transparency as unnamed man is in serious but stable condition at hospital</p><p>A US Immigration and Customs Enforcement (<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ice-us-immigration-and-customs-enforcement\">ICE</a>) officer shot and wounded a man on Sunday afternoon in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas\">Texas</a>’s capital of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/austin\">Austin</a>, local authorities said, and anti-ICE protesters quickly gathered at the scene.</p><p>The unnamed man was in serious but stable condition at a hospital after being shot once in the torso on the city’s north side, Austin’s police chief, Lisa Davis, said at a news conference with the mayor and other city officials.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/20/man-shot-ice-agent-austin-texas\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
